From e524c21d0ef6733b4de9d886890e73bed8e19589 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:50:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] Claude Code plugin: clippings

A code review in a workgroup files its findings as clippings, as in
iTerm2, kept by the workgroup's Chat session:

- it2 gains `session add-clipping TYPE TITLE DETAIL` and
  `session archive-clippings`, and accepts a session named by all of
  $TERM_SESSION_ID as well as by what follows its first colon. The D-Bus
  object gains addClipping, archiveClippings and clippings.
- The review runs with iTerm2's code review system prompt, which tells
  it to archive the last round and file each finding with it2, and with
  settings that let it run those two commands without asking.
- The Claude Clippings panel (Ctrl+Shift+F4) shows the findings of the
  workgroup in view and opens when new ones arrive. Send to Chat pastes
  the selected findings, or all, into Chat as a bracketed paste without
  submitting, archives them and switches to Chat; Archive archives.
- Send Review Findings to Chat Automatically (off by default,
  [ClaudeCode] AutoSendClippings): when the review goes from working to
  finished and Chat is not working, its findings are pasted into Chat,
  submitted half a second later, archived, and Chat is shown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
